Hi All,

  I've got a B+W 500 Mhz G3 system running the 2.4.10-pre8 linuxppc_2_4_devel
kernel from bk and I'm continuing to see random seg faults.

  I can't even do a complete kernel build without gcc taking a seg fault. Oddily
enough if I put the packaged YDL 2 kernel (2.2.19) things are just fine.
Unfortunately the 2.2.19 token ring support is hosed, so I need to be on 2.4 on
this box to do anything useful with it.

  Wish I had time to track this down but other duties call.

  Enclosed is the config that I'm using.

  Paul, if you want I can give you a user id on this system and you could ssh to
it if you like.

  Regards,

  Tom
